<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann, AT&amp;T, Unisource agree Arcor links.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann, AT&amp;T, Unisource agree Arcor links.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering firm Mannesmann AG said on Thursday it had reached a fixed agreement with AT&amp;T and Unisource on a partnership in Arcor, Mannesmann's telecom venture with Deutsche Bahn AG.</p>
<p>In a mandatory statement, the company said AT&amp;T, Unisource and Deutsche Bank AG had agreed to take stakes in the Arcor consortium, which owns 49.8 percent of the group. The agreement was subject to cartel authority approval.</p>
<p>AT&amp;T and Unisource would each take 15 percent and Deutsche Bank AG would take 10 percent, Mannesmann said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
